# UI-PLACE-1: the construction menu's pickaxe and a building chosen while demolishing, as the
# original's (GOG Wine runner, cache/orig/ui-place-1, docs/re/ui.md 2.6). The pickaxe with nothing
# armed turns the demolish mode on (p2_pickaxe_nothing_armed); clicked again, nothing is armed
# (p2_pickaxe_off). With the pickaxe on, the pioneer house cell opens its panel and the demolish
# mode is off (p2_demolish_then_501). The cancel-X closes the panel and keeps the house armed
# (p1_a_after_x), so a map click then builds it on the tile construction_menu_arm.script proves
# free for type 501. Before the fix the pickaxe did nothing with nothing armed, and a cell chosen
# while demolishing left the tool demolishing (owner test ui_4.mp4, 2026-11-15).
# Launch: --play data/maps/lan5.txt --construction-menu on --layout data/ui
resize 1024 768
wait frames 5
look 1140 516
key b
wait frames 5
expect fact tool.mode == off
click_px 996 736
wait frames 3
expect title tool: demolish
expect fact tool.mode == demolish
click_px 996 736
wait frames 3
expect fact tool.mode == off
expect title-lacks tool:
click 1156 516
wait frames 10
expect outcome none
click_px 996 736
wait frames 3
expect fact tool.mode == demolish
click_px 833 330
wait frames 5
expect title build 501
expect title-lacks demolish
expect fact tool.mode == build
click_px 1000 742
wait frames 3
expect title build 501
expect fact tool.mode == build
# One selection click so far: the map click with nothing armed. No chrome click reached the map.
expect fact selection.clicks == 1
click 1156 516
wait outcome
expect outcome Applied
quit
